  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Added `start_in_air: bool` to `cl::ThreadCycle` and `ThreadCycleDto` (defaults to `false`).\n- Added optional `AIR 1` flag to `THREAD` records in `crates/post/src/post/cnc_thread.rs` and exposed it to post scripts as `properties.StartInAir`.\n- Refused G76 by name in `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps` (`g76Why`) whenever `p.StartInAir !== true`.\n- Added `cycle_infeed_band` and `part_band_clear` in `crates/motion/src/turning/thread_cycle.rs` to check the full rapid-infeed axial band `[min(start_s, s_deep) - insert_width/2, max(start_s, s_deep) + insert_width/2]` against the part silhouette and raw stock.\n- Added `crates/app/src/operation/g76_start.rs` to refine `start_in_air` against the revolved part, revolved stock and prior Facing, Grooving, Turning and Drilling operations (`TurnedAhead` now carries grooving blade half-width `band`).\n- Updated `crates/motion/src/turning/thread.rs` and `crates/motion/src/turning/revolve.rs` so a threading pass can start in free air in front of a free end face without false out-of-domain rest warnings.\n- Updated the Fanuc G76 test bar fixtures and three golden `.nc` files to start in free air (`Z16.` / `Z16.625` / `Z0.6299`) instead of inside a solid `Z=40` bar.\n- Recorded the design choice in `docs/decisions/2878-fanuc-g76-start-in-air.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nA Fanuc-type G76 cycle moves the insert from the start point to each pass depth at rapid traverse. Previously, `fanuc-lathe.cps` emitted G76 without checking whether the start point stood in free air, and `turning::thread` clamped pass starts to the part silhouette domain. As a result, G76 started inside solid material (for example at `Z77.4` inside a `Z=78` end face on the cone-thread part).\n\n## Tests\n\n### Pinning tests (red before fix, green after fix)\n\n- `lathe_post_g76_start::g76_refuses_when_start_point_is_inside_a_solid_bar` (G76 refused by name, G32 still posts)\n- `lathe_post_g76_start::g76_refuses_on_cone_thread_start_inside_end_face` (reproduces #2878 cone-thread part)\n- `lathe_post_g76_start::g76_posts_when_start_point_is_in_free_air_in_front_of_end_face`\n- `lathe_post_g76_start::g76_refuses_uncut_stock_in_front_of_end_face_and_posts_after_facing`\n- `lathe_post_g76_start::g76_refuses_legacy_stream_without_air_flag`\n- `camcraft-app::operation::g76_start::tests::relief_groove_wider_than_insert_passes_when_grooved_and_refuses_when_uncut_or_narrow`\n- `camcraft-app::operation::g76_start::tests::flank_infeed_refuses_when_deep_pass_overlaps_end_face`\n- `turning_thread_cycle::start_in_air_distinguishes_solid_bar_from_free_end_start`\n\n### Mutation checks\n\n- Removed `p.StartInAir !== true` guard in `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps`: 4 of 5 tests in `lathe_post_g76_start` failed (red), then passed after restore (green).\n- Disabled `g76_start::judge` in `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`: `g76_refuses_uncut_stock_in_front_of_end_face_and_posts_after_facing` failed (red), then passed after restore (green).\n- Restored post-retain `lat.push(w0); lat.push(w1);` in `crates/motion/src/turning/revolve.rs`: `g76_posts_when_start_point_is_in_free_air_in_front_of_end_face` failed with `6.0000 mm rest` (red), then passed after restore (green).\n- Forced `start_in_air = true` in `crates/motion/src/turning/thread_cycle.rs`: `start_in_air_distinguishes_solid_bar_from_free_end_start` failed (red), then passed after restore (green).\n\n### Gate and clippy\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` (fell back to batch because `crates/cl` changed): 955 steps, 0 failed (includes `clippy -D warnings`).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-cl -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: 0 warnings.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/fanuc-lathe/thread_g76.nc`: `G00 X12.1 Z14.` -> `G00 X12.1 Z16.` (start point moved into free air past the free end face).\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/fanuc-lathe/thread_g76_area.nc`: `G00 X12.1 Z14.625` -> `G00 X12.1 Z16.625` (flank-infeed start point moved into free air past the free end face).\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/inch/fanuc-lathe/thread_g76.nc`: `G00 X0.4764 Z0.5512` -> `G00 X0.4764 Z0.6299` (inch start point moved into free air past the free end face).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Execution on a physical Fanuc lathe control or third-party Fanuc simulator.\n- `assets/posts/tormach-lathe.cps` G76 refusal (out of scope for #2878; can reuse `properties.StartInAir` in a follow-up).\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`: touches the same file, different function/arm as open PRs #2853, #2836, #2833, #2831, #2822, #2716, #2714, #2678; whichever merges second refreshes.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/mod.rs`: touches the same file, different module declaration as open PRs #2853, #2836, #2833, #2716, #2714, #2678; whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Refuse Fanuc lathe G76 cycles whose start point stands above material and allow free-air starts in front of the end face or in a relief groove wider than the insert.\nEffort: high\nFixes #2878\n",
